Fix or-tools 9.15 Gurobi dynamic loading (google/or-tools#5079 + dlclose
use-after-free). math_opt never triggers LoadGurobiDynamicLibrary (empty
GRB* std::function globals -> bad_function_call), and DynamicLibrary's
implicit copy + dlclose'ing destructor unloads libgurobi when the
NoDestructor init lambda's return value is not elided (unoptimized
builds) -> bound pointers dangle -> segfault. Applied with `patch -p1`
inside the or-tools source tree.

Upstream PR google/or-tools#5272 fixes the same two bugs on the way to
Gurobi 13 support, but is written against a post-9.15 main: it spells the
macros ABSL_RETURN_IF_ERROR/ABSL_ASSIGN_OR_RETURN, targets a refactored
two-argument Gurobi::New, and deletes DynamicLibrary's move constructor
that 9.15's gurobi_environment.cc needs (it initializes the library from
a by-value lambda return). It therefore does not apply to 9.15. Drop this
patch once that PR lands in a release we bump to.

--- a/ortools/math_opt/solvers/gurobi/g_gurobi.cc	2026-07-31 18:48:29.849262445 +0200
+++ b/ortools/math_opt/solvers/gurobi/g_gurobi.cc	2026-07-31 18:48:29.862845769 +0200
@@ -161,6 +161,10 @@
 
 absl::StatusOr<GRBenvUniquePtr> GurobiNewPrimaryEnv(
     const std::optional<GurobiIsvKey>& isv_key) {
+  // The GRB* function table is populated by the dynamic-library loader,
+  // which nothing on the MathOpt path invokes (google/or-tools#5079);
+  // without this call every GRB* std::function global is empty.
+  RETURN_IF_ERROR(LoadGurobiDynamicLibrary({}));
   if (isv_key.has_value()) {
     ASSIGN_OR_RETURN(GRBenv* const naked_primary_env,
                      NewPrimaryEnvFromISVKey(*isv_key));
